{
  "quest.3C3122DF5C0EA192.title": "And Now?",
  "quest.3C3122DF5C0EA192.quest_subtitle": "The guided course ends here; your own world begins",
  "quest.3C3122DF5C0EA192.quest_desc": [
    "You survived the first nights, built dependable supplies, crossed the Nether, defeated the Ender Dragon, returned from an End City, and learned to fly safely. You are ready to explore without a prescribed route.",
    "",
    "Minecraft has no single final task. Choose a direction, prepare for the hazards you know, record the way home, observe before acting, and retreat while you can still choose how. Bringing yourself and your discoveries home matters more than clearing every room.",
    "",
    "The surrounding cards name major places and dangers that First Torch has not turned into full quest lines. They are optional reading, not a completion list. Nothing depends on completing them, and you do not need to visit these places to finish the course.",
    "",
    "Set the checkmark when you are ready to choose your own next goal.",
  ],
  "task.72C95CCAFC3F3A16.title": "Ready to choose an independent goal",

  "quest.009D0C9674747314.title": "Temples and Archaeology",
  "quest.009D0C9674747314.quest_subtitle": "Desert Pyramids, Jungle Temples, and buried Trail Ruins",
  "quest.009D0C9674747314.quest_desc": [
    "Desert Pyramids hide a treasure chamber beneath the central floor. The Stone Pressure Plate below can ignite TNT. Never drop onto the centre pattern; dig a staircase from the side, expose the chamber carefully, and remove the plate from a safe position before opening Chests. Use a Brush on Suspicious Sand instead of breaking it.",
    "",
    "Jungle Temples contain Tripwires connected to Arrow Dispensers. Look for String and Tripwire Hooks, block the firing direction, and disarm the traps before approaching Chests. Their lever puzzle opens another hidden space. Light the rooms and check corners before using a container.",
    "",
    "Trail Ruins are mostly buried. Make a controlled staircase and use a Brush on Suspicious Gravel; breaking suspicious blocks destroys the hidden item. Watch for falling Gravel, caves, darkness, and mobs while uncovering the structure.",
    "",
    "The checkmark only marks this card as read. No visit is required.",
  ],
  "task.25B14938B9673B9F.title": "Read the temple and archaeology warnings",

  "quest.419FC369AD620958.title": "Oceans and Buried Routes",
  "quest.419FC369AD620958.quest_subtitle": "Shipwrecks, Ocean Ruins, Buried Treasure, and Monuments",
  "quest.419FC369AD620958.quest_desc": [
    "Shipwrecks and Ocean Ruins may lead to treasure maps, but Drowned, limited air, poor visibility, and long swims can trap an unprepared explorer. Bring a Boat, food, spare blocks, and a planned shore return. Respiration and Water Breathing make deeper searches much safer.",
    "",
    "Buried Treasure is usually near a coast. Secure the area and dig a broad stair or shallow pit instead of dropping into a narrow hole where Water, Sand, or mobs can trap you.",
    "",
    "Ocean Monuments are guarded by Guardians and Elder Guardians. Their beams reward breaking line of sight, and the elders apply Mining Fatigue. Milk removes the effect temporarily, but a living elder can apply it again. Treat a Monument as a prepared expedition with underwater breathing, cover, a marked exit, and a retreat plan.",
    "",
    "The checkmark only marks this card as read. No visit is required.",
  ],
  "task.7AFF2F0410BF29E9.title": "Read the ocean exploration warnings",

  "quest.5AFE972108C13B48.title": "Raiders and Woodland Mansions",
  "quest.5AFE972108C13B48.quest_subtitle": "Crossbows, raids, Vindicators, Evokers, and Vexes",
  "quest.5AFE972108C13B48.quest_desc": [
    "Pillager Outposts place you against groups of crossbow users with long sightlines. Observe from cover, keep a clear retreat route, and avoid pulling the whole structure at once. Do not drink an Ominous Bottle near a Village unless you deliberately want to risk starting a Raid.",
    "",
    "Woodland Mansions are large, dark, and easy to become lost inside. Vindicators deal heavy Axe damage. Evokers attack through the floor and summon small flying Vexes that can pass through blocks; defeating an Evoker can yield a Totem of Undying. Mark every cleared junction and return outside between sections.",
    "",
    "Both structures are optional. Bring strong armour, Shield, ranged attacks, light, food, blocks, and a Bed placed safely well away from the structure.",
    "",
    "The checkmark only marks this card as read. No visit is required.",
  ],
  "task.50225BFAFB16F710.title": "Read the raider and mansion warnings",

  "quest.0BF75245596E6948.title": "Trial Chambers",
  "quest.0BF75245596E6948.quest_subtitle": "Underground combat rooms built from Tuff and Copper",
  "quest.0BF75245596E6948.quest_desc": [
    "Trial Chambers contain linked rooms, traps, Vaults, and Trial Spawners that release combat waves according to nearby players. Breezes use wind attacks with strong knockback, so edges, pits, and exposed approaches matter as much as direct damage.",
    "",
    "Clear and mark one room at a time. Build a protected recovery point outside the active room, keep food and ranged options ready, and learn the safe return before activating more spawners. Trial Keys open ordinary Vaults for player-specific rewards.",
    "",
    "Ominous Bottles can turn this into the harder ominous version through the Bad Omen and Trial Omen system. Save that choice until the ordinary chamber and its exits are understood.",
    "",
    "The checkmark only marks this card as read. No visit is required.",
  ],
  "task.37C1C4C9A054B116.title": "Read the Trial Chamber warnings",

  "quest.30C7BD69EB7BE641.title": "The Ancient City and the Warden",
  "quest.30C7BD69EB7BE641.quest_subtitle": "The 'lost city' is real, deep underground, and built around avoiding detection",
  "quest.30C7BD69EB7BE641.quest_desc": [
    "Its proper name is the Ancient City. It lies in the Deep Dark, where Sculk Sensors react to vibrations and Sculk Shriekers can build warnings that eventually summon a Warden. Sneak, use Wool to block or dampen vibration paths, and avoid opening containers, placing blocks, or breaking blocks near active sensors until you understand the route.",
    "",
    "The Warden is a survival hazard rather than a boss to defeat. It follows vibrations and scent, causes Darkness, and its sonic attack passes through blocks. A pillar or small box is not reliable protection. If a Shrieker warns you, stop creating vibrations and retreat along the prepared route before another warning occurs.",
    "",
    "Bring Wool, food, healing, projectiles that can distract at a distance, and a clearly marked exit. Leave valuable gear at a safe staging point. The safest successful Ancient City trip may end without opening a single Chest.",
    "",
    "The checkmark only marks this card as read. No visit is required, and summoning a Warden is never required.",
  ],
  "task.0AB3D6E206DBD2DD.title": "Read the Ancient City and Warden warnings",

  "quest.23B4200152D3EAE9.title": "Your World, Your Goals",
  "quest.23B4200152D3EAE9.quest_subtitle": "Bosses, projects, discoveries, and the freedom to stop or begin again",
  "quest.23B4200152D3EAE9.quest_desc": [
    "You can summon the Wither with Soul Sand or Soul Soil and three Wither Skeleton Skulls, but its birth explosion, Wither effect, and destructive movement make it dangerous to every nearby build. Never summon it at home. The Ender Dragon can also be summoned again with End Crystals placed around the exit portal.",
    "",
    "You can search for more End Cities, map rare biomes, complete advancements, learn Redstone, automate farms, build roads and railways, restore structures, collect every music disc, or create a base that only you would have imagined. Multiplayer can turn the same world into a shared story.",
    "",
    "Use the habits behind every First Torch lesson: prepare enough to survive a mistake, change one thing at a time, keep a route home, and stop when the situation becomes unclear. From here, curiosity chooses the lesson.",
    "",
    "The checkmark only marks this card as read. The course is already complete.",
  ],
  "task.0ACB79CC7F3DEFEF.title": "Chose a personal direction for the world",
}
